      "anchor": {
        "mission_intent": "We need a full systems security engineering specification for the Supply process activities on our next-generation satellite ground control platform (Project Meridian). The spec must address how our organization, acting as a supplier, ensures that security properties are preserved in every product and service deliverable provided to the acquiring agency. Specifically, the document should cover supply agreement security provisions aligned with ISO/IEC/IEEE 15288 Section 6.1.1.3 and the supply-chain risk management guidance in ISO/IEC 27036, and it should reference the Systems Security Engineering framework from NIST SP 800-160 Volume 1 Chapter 3 throughout. Include detailed requirements for transition, operation, and validation activities that ensure security is maintained during system handoff and acceptance by the acquirer or their designated representative. The specification must define supplier security assurance evidence packages, traceability from acquirer security requirements through design and implementation artifacts, and acceptance criteria that the acquirer's validation team can independently verify. Ensure the document addresses a multidisciplinary engineering approach to trustworthiness, incorporating protection needs from both the acquirer's mission context and our internal secure development lifecycle aligned with ISO/IEC 12207 and capability maturity practices per ISO/IEC 21827. Please have a draft ready for review by the end of next sprint.",
